    "title": "Driver killed in head-on crash involving stolen car in Ingleside, sheriff says - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By ABC7 Chicago Digital Team ,\n13 hours ago A driver died on Wednesday morning while driving a stolen car, according to the Lake County Sheriff's Office.\nABC7 Chicago is now streaming 24/7. Click here to watch The crash happened at about 5 a.m. on Route 134 east of North Catherine Street, officials said.\nThe driver of a Honda sedan was driving westbound on Route 134, when he allegedly veered into the eastbound lanes and crashed head-on with a GMC work truck.\nChopper 7 was over the scene.\nThe driver of the Honda died at the scene.\nSheriff deputies said the Honda was reported stolen from a gym in Fox Lake. The driver allegedly has an open bottle of whiskey in his lap at the time of the crash.\nThe driver of the GMC is a 44-year-old man from Johnsburg. He was taken to an area hospital and is expected to be OK.\nClosures were in place as police investigated.\n18",
